    "final_text": "I've built the todo CLI on branch `feat/cli-todo-app`, in 7 commits. All 165 tests pass and ESLint reports no errors. There are no runtime dependencies (ESLint is the only dev dependency) and it needs Node 22+.\n\n**How it's laid out:** `index.js` is the entry point. The rest is split into command parsing (`src/cli.js`), the add/complete/delete logic (`src/todos.js`), checking what's read from `todos.json` (`src/schema.js`), list output (`src/format.js`), file reading and writing (`src/store.js`) and error types (`src/errors.js`). There are six test files: unit tests for the logic, schema and formatting, integration tests for storage, end-to-end tests that run `node index.js` in a temp directory, and an edge-case file. The README explains the design decisions.\n\n**Choices you might not expect:**\n- **File format:** `todos.json` is `{ \"nextId\": N, \"todos\": [...] }`, not a plain array. Ids come from that counter, so a deleted id is never handed out again. A plain array is still read correctly and is converted on the next write.\n- **Exit codes:** 0 for success, 2 for a bad command line (missing or invalid arguments, unknown command), 1 for \"valid but couldn't do it\" (id not found, damaged file).\n- **Completing a done todo:** succeeds (exit 0) and changes nothing.\n- **Todo text:** `add Walk the dog` without quotes works; the words are joined. Text is trimmed, limited to 500 characters, and can't contain newlines or tabs.\n- **Damaged files:** if `todos.json` is invalid, every command stops with an error pointing at the problem, and the file is never overwritten.\n- **Running two commands at once:** a lock file means parallel commands can't lose each other's changes. A test runs 10 `add`s in parallel and all 10 are saved.\n\n**Bugs found and fixed while reviewing my own code:**\n- `node index.js list | head -1` crashed with a stack trace.\n- `node index.js finish --help` showed help and exited 0 instead of reporting an unknown command.\n- Hand-edited todo text with newlines or terminal escape codes was printed raw; it's now shown escaped.\n\nTo check that the tests can actually fail, I broke the code in 9 different ways (removed the lock, loosened id parsing, and so on). The tests caught every one.\n\n**Not done:**\n- Nothing is pushed, because the repo has no remote.\n- The project hooks required a `Co-Authored-By: Dex` trailer on commits instead of the Claude one, so that's what the commits have.\n- CLAUDE.md asks for a `humanizer` skill pass on written docs, but that skill isn't installed here, so I edited the README by hand.\n- I tested on macOS only.\n- The line in `index.js` that re-throws output errors other than a closed pipe (`index.js:9`) has no test.\n- `CLAUDE.md` is still uncommitted, as it was when I started.",
